{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"0a32e33a19f056bd","name":"card_unit_1e_bfl","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/France/units/card_unit_1e_bfl","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"1re BFL","text":"Deployment: Deal damage to the enemy HQ equal to the number of non-French units you control.","flavorText":"The 1re BFL was a brigade of the 1st Free French Division (French 1re Division Française Libre, 1re DFL) during WWII. Led by General Charles de Gaulle, the 1re Free French Division initially consisted of volunteers from various French colonies and territories, as well as French soldiers who had escaped from occupied France. The division saw action in several major campaigns and battles throughout the war and played a key role in liberating French territories in North Africa and later Europe. In the North African Campaign the division participated in the Battle of Bir Hakeim from 26 May – 11 June 1942, then in the Second Battle of El Alamein, and in both battles the 1re BFL distinguished itself. In 1943, the 1re Free French Division participated in the Italian campaign, fighting in battles such as the Battle of Monte Cassino. The division continued to engage in combat across Italy, contributing to the Allied advance and the liberation of Rome. During the invasion of France in 1944, the 1re Free French Division played a crucial role in the liberation of Paris. They were among the first units to enter the French capital, symbolizing the restoration of French sovereignty and the end of German occupation. The division went on to fight in other significant battles, including the Battle of Alsace and the Battle of Authion, as part of the Allied efforts on the Western Front. They also participated in the final offensive in Germany, contributing to the ultimate victory in Europe.","faction":"France","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":1,"attack":5,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_1e_bfl","title":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_1e_bfl_title","SourceString":"1re BFL","LocalizedString":"1re BFL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":5,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::France","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_1e_bfl_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Deal damage to the enemy HQ equal to the number of non-French units you control.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Deal damage to the enemy HQ equal to the number of non-French units you control."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_france","Key":"card_unit_1e_bfl_history","SourceString":"The 1re BFL was a brigade of the 1st Free French Division (French 1re Division Française Libre, 1re DFL) during WWII. Led by General Charles de Gaulle, the 1re Free French Division initially consisted of volunteers from various French colonies and territories, as well as French soldiers who had escaped from occupied France. The division saw action in several major campaigns and battles throughout the war and played a key role in liberating French territories in North Africa and later Europe. In the North African Campaign the division participated in the Battle of Bir Hakeim from 26 May – 11 June 1942, then in the Second Battle of El Alamein, and in both battles the 1re BFL distinguished itself. In 1943, the 1re Free French Division participated in the Italian campaign, fighting in battles such as the Battle of Monte Cassino. The division continued to engage in combat across Italy, contributing to the Allied advance and the liberation of Rome. During the invasion of France in 1944, the 1re Free French Division played a crucial role in the liberation of Paris. They were among the first units to enter the French capital, symbolizing the restoration of French sovereignty and the end of German occupation. The division went on to fight in other significant battles, including the Battle of Alsace and the Battle of Authion, as part of the Allied efforts on the Western Front. They also participated in the final offensive in Germany, contributing to the ultimate victory in Europe.","LocalizedString":"The 1re BFL was a brigade of the 1st Free French Division (French 1re Division Française Libre, 1re DFL) during WWII. Led by General Charles de Gaulle, the 1re Free French Division initially consisted of volunteers from various French colonies and territories, as well as French soldiers who had escaped from occupied France. The division saw action in several major campaigns and battles throughout the war and played a key role in liberating French territories in North Africa and later Europe. In the North African Campaign the division participated in the Battle of Bir Hakeim from 26 May – 11 June 1942, then in the Second Battle of El Alamein, and in both battles the 1re BFL distinguished itself. In 1943, the 1re Free French Division participated in the Italian campaign, fighting in battles such as the Battle of Monte Cassino. The division continued to engage in combat across Italy, contributing to the Allied advance and the liberation of Rome. During the invasion of France in 1944, the 1re Free French Division played a crucial role in the liberation of Paris. They were among the first units to enter the French capital, symbolizing the restoration of French sovereignty and the end of German occupation. The division went on to fight in other significant battles, including the Battle of Alsace and the Battle of Authion, as part of the Allied efforts on the Western Front. They also participated in the final offensive in Germany, contributing to the ultimate victory in Europe."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Small'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Small.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/France/Spring2023